NAME
    picview - graphical image viewer

SYNOPSIS
picview [file]
 
 DESCRIPTION
    A tiny image viewer for the VNU desktop. Without an argument it
    walks the /etc/vnu/pics directory; with a file argument (as the files
    manager supplies when you open a .png/.jpg/.jpeg) it decodes and
    shows just that file. Either way, BMP, PNG and JPEG are decoded
    with the embedded px.h decoder and rendered into the window's
    client area in the display's own colours. A display attached to a
    virtio-gpu shows 24 bits per pixel and the picture is drawn as it
    is; a VBE display has 16 colours behind a DAC, so the same picture
    is quantised to the nearest of them (dithered unless `d` says not
    to), which is the only thing about it that loses anything. The
    program asks the display which case it is in rather than deciding.
    A file dropped onto the window (drag it from the file manager)
    switches it to that file, like a file argument would.

KEYS
    [ ]   previous / next picture (gallery mode only)
    z     toggle zoom (fit window / 1:1)
    d     toggle ordered dithering (a 16-colour display only; on a
          24-bit one the picture is already finer than 16 steps)
    Esc   close the window (opened from the file manager: return to it)

FILES
    /etc/vnu/pics   directory of embedded demo pictures
    /apps/picview/bin   the program itself
